# board.pdl - Chutes and Ladders: the track as DATA for the shared engine game_core (ledger kind). The first ledger row records the hash of this file and rules.pdl:
# editing either after a game began makes every verb refuse that ledger (start a new game).
#
# ############################################################################################################################################
# THE JUMP TABLE BELOW IS FROM MEMORY OF THE COMMON US BOARD (2026-11-09). IT HAS NOT BEEN CHECKED AGAINST AN OFFICIAL BOARD OR RULE SHEET.
# Check every row before this ruleset is called "the classic one". (The name "Chutes and Ladders" is a trademark; the public game is "Snakes and Ladders": the owner picks the shipped title.)
# ############################################################################################################################################
#
# TRACK | length | N                squares 1..N; everybody starts on 0 (off the board); the finish rule is rules.pdl RULE finish
# JUMP  | from | to | kind | id      landing on `from` moves you to `to` (kind ladder goes up, chute goes down; the engine only looks at the first two fields). No chains: no jump may start where another ends (case chutes checks it).
# BOARD | cols | rows | path        the geometry the PAGE will draw (10 x 10, serpentine: row 1 runs left to right 1..10, row 2 right to left 11..20, ... so 100 is the top LEFT). The engine ignores these rows; the page needs a `page` verb (not built).
# TALK  | up|down | words           the words of the table-talk sentence ("B rolled 4 and climbed the ladder from 28 to 84")
TRACK | length | 100
BOARD | cols   | 10
BOARD | rows   | 10
BOARD | path   | serpentine
TALK  | up     | climbed the ladder
TALK  | down   | slid down the chute
# ladders (9)
JUMP | 1  | 38  | ladder | L1
JUMP | 4  | 14  | ladder | L2
JUMP | 9  | 31  | ladder | L3
JUMP | 21 | 42  | ladder | L4
JUMP | 28 | 84  | ladder | L5
JUMP | 36 | 44  | ladder | L6
JUMP | 51 | 67  | ladder | L7
JUMP | 71 | 91  | ladder | L8
JUMP | 80 | 100 | ladder | L9
# chutes (10)
JUMP | 16 | 6   | chute  | C1
JUMP | 47 | 26  | chute  | C2
JUMP | 49 | 11  | chute  | C3
JUMP | 56 | 53  | chute  | C4
JUMP | 62 | 19  | chute  | C5
JUMP | 64 | 60  | chute  | C6
JUMP | 87 | 24  | chute  | C7
JUMP | 93 | 73  | chute  | C8
JUMP | 95 | 75  | chute  | C9
JUMP | 98 | 78  | chute  | C10
